    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0212" n="186" xml:id="pg186"/>

                <head>70. Telegram From the Embassy in Vietnam to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="1" xml:id="d70-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Saigon</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1963-03-30T12:00:00+08:00">March 30, 1963,
                        noon</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>860. CINCPAC for POLAD. Deptel 911<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d70-f2"/> greatly appreciated. If Thuan has been unable to overcome main objection to
                    counterinsurgency fund described Embtel
                        852<anchor n="3" xml:id="d70-f3"/> on basis arguments already advanced,
                    warnings and assurances contained reftel
                    should be most useful in my next meeting with him, Nhu or Diem. To make
                    point even more emphatic, plan tell them also that further procurement and
                    shipment of hamlet kit materials (barbed wire, etc.),PL 480 and AID dollar procurement
                    items for hamlets would not seem justified unless there is adequate piaster fund
                    to go with them, and agreed procedures for their effective use.</p>
                <p>Harkin and Brent concur.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Nolting</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
